// ── basic_stringstream<CharT,Traits,Allocator> [stringstream] ───────────
// Unlike istringstream/ostringstream, stringstream's ctors do NOT force any
// extra bits into `which` -- verified against [stringstream]'s Effects
// clauses verbatim (e.g. "_sb_ with basic_stringbuf<...>(which)", no OR at
// all): a real, standard-mandated asymmetry. The class has no single
// "primary direction" to force the way istringstream forces `in` and
// ostringstream forces `out` -- its own DEFAULT argument already carries
// both bits, so an explicit-which caller who really wants neither gets
